  "description": "Ananas comosus var. microstachys (synonym: Ananas nanus), commonly known as Dwarf Pineapple or Mini Pineapple, is a small bromeliad native to tropical South America (Brazil, Paraguay). It belongs to the Bromeliaceae family and features a rosette of stiff, spiny, green to bronze leaves (up to 15 cm long) in a pineapple-like form. It produces a small, ornamental pineapple fruit (3-5 cm) that is edible but not as sweet as commercial pineapples. Upright, rosette-forming habit to about 15 cm; small purple to red flowers before fruiting. Terrestrial in well-draining soils in the wild. In terrariums it adds vibrant interest with its miniature pineapple form. It's popular among bromeliad enthusiasts for its compact size and ornamental fruit.",
